+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+Native Windows ARM64 (`aarch64`) build of GNU tar 1.35 (with the MSYS2 patches) for the
+MSYS2 `usr/bin` layer of Git for Windows, on branch `arm64-port`.
+
+The target is the MSYS2 runtime on ARM64 (`aarch64-pc-cygwin`, `msys-2.0.dll`), built
+with the `aarch64-pc-cygwin` GCC cross toolchain. It is not an MSVC target. MSVC is used
+only for `dumpbin`.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- `build-aux/config.guess`: added an `aarch64:CYGWIN*:*:*` case that returns
+  `aarch64-pc-cygwin`. It sits next to the existing `i*`/`x86_64` Cygwin cases.
+  - This case is only reached when `uname -s` reports `CYGWIN_NT*`, which means a genuine
+    Cygwin runtime.
+  - The ARM64 MSYS2 runtime reports `MSYS_NT-10.0-26100 aarch64`. That already guesses
+    `aarch64-pc-msys` without this change, as verified with the ARM64 `sh`/`uname`.
+  - Cross builds pass `--host` and are not affected.
+  - The MSYS2 recipe runs `autoreconf -fi`, which replaces this file.
+### Source Code
+None. No x86 SIMD intrinsics and no inline assembly.
+- The `__asm__` hits are only `__REDIRECT`/`__ASMNAME` symbol renames.
+- The arch guards (`gnu/float.c`, `gnu/float.in.h`, `gnu/signal.in.h`, `gnu/unistd.in.h`)
+  already fall through to correct generic paths for `__aarch64__`.
+### CI/CD
+None. The repository has no CI configuration.
+### New Files
+- `ARM64-PORT.md` (this file)
+- `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt` (timing baseline)
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites:
+- MSYS2 at `C:\msys64` with the `aarch64-pc-cygwin` cross toolchain (GCC 17.0.0 20260828,
+  binutils 2.47.50).
+- An ARM64 sysroot at `/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin` that contains `msys-2.0.dll`, libiconv,
+  libintl and `sh`.
+- `crossarm64/config.site` from MSYS2-packages, so that configure runs its checks
+  natively instead of guessing.
+
+### Build
+```bash
+MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc '
+  mkdir -p /c/wos-eval/work/tar/build-arm64 && cd /c/wos-eval/work/tar/build-arm64
+  export PATH="$PATH:/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin"
+  export CONFIG_SITE=/home/HCKTest/MSYS2-packages/crossarm64/config.site
+  export gl_cv_have_weak=no
+  CC=aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc AR=aarch64-pc-cygwin-ar RANLIB=aarch64-pc-cygwin-ranlib \
+  CFLAGS="-O2 -pipe --param=ggc-min-heapsize=2000000 --param=ggc-min-expand=1000" \
+  CPPFLAGS="-I/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/include" LDFLAGS="-L/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/lib" \
+  ../configure --build=x86_64-pc-cygwin --host=aarch64-pc-cygwin --prefix=/usr \
+    --sbindir=/usr/bin --libexecdir=/usr/lib/tar --enable-backup-scripts --disable-gcc-warnings
+  make -j8'
+```
+- Build output: `build-arm64/src/tar.exe`, `build-arm64/rmt/rmt.exe`, and the backup
+  scripts in `build-arm64/scripts`.
+- The `ggc` params work around a garbage-collector hang in the cross `cc1`.
+- configure guessed only one check ("unlink of a parent directory"). It found iconv
+  (`-liconv`) and NLS (`-lintl`) in the sysroot.
+- `tar.exe` imports `msys-2.0.dll`, `msys-iconv-2.dll`, `msys-intl-8.dll` and `KERNEL32.dll`.
+
+### Run Tests
+The test helpers are built with the x64 make. The suite is then run by the ARM64 shell,
+so the ARM64 runtime owns every process.
+```bash
+MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cd /c/wos-eval/work/tar/build-arm64 && export PATH="$PATH:/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin" && make -C tests genfile.exe checkseekhole.exe ckmtime.exe atconfig atlocal'
+# inside the ARM64 bash (/c/msys64/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin/bash.exe), with MSYSTEM=MSYS and
+# PATH=<build>/src:<build>/tests:<build>/rmt:/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin
+cd /c/wos-eval/work/tar/build-arm64/tests && SHELL=/usr/bin/sh CONFIG_SHELL=/usr/bin/sh /usr/bin/sh ../../tests/testsuite -j8
+```
+- Set `SHELL`/`CONFIG_SHELL` inside the ARM64 shell. If you set them in Git Bash, Git Bash
+  rewrites the POSIX paths.
+- Expected result: 198 passed, 10 failed, 36 skipped. This matches the x64 MSYS2 tar
+  exactly; see Test Results.
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+tar has no benchmark suite. The timing baseline was produced with these ad-hoc scripts:
+- `C:\wos-eval\work\tar-scratch\bench\mktree.sh`: builds 2000 x 100 KiB files (196 MiB).
+- `C:\wos-eval\work\tar-scratch\bench\bench.sh`: runs `tar -cf`, `-xf`, `-czf` and
+  `-xzf` three times each.
+
+The result is `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`.
+
+## Test Results
+- **Build host**: native ARM64 (Snapdragon X Elite X1E80100, Windows 11 build 26100).
+- **Executed**: yes, under the ARM64 runtime. Inside the test shell, `uname -m` =
+  `aarch64` and `tar` = `build-arm64/src/tar`.
+- **Passed**: 198  **Failed**: 10  **Skipped**: 36 (244 tests; 208 run). Taken from
+  `build-arm64/tests/testsuite.log`.
+- **x64 reference**: MSYS2 `/usr/bin/tar.exe` 1.35, same recipe, full run.
+  - 198 / 10 / 36, with an identical list of failing tests.
+  - After normalising paths and timestamps, the failure output is identical.
+
+None of the 10 failures is ARM64-specific. All of them are Windows/MSYS environment
+behaviour:
+
+| # | Test | Cause (same on x64) |
+|---|---|---|
+| 35 | T-null2 | Windows filenames cannot contain `:` or `\` |
+| 89 | extrac06 | `noacl` permission emulation (got 755, expected 777) |
+| 106 | extrac23 | `noacl` permission emulation |
+| 96 | extrac13 | Default MSYS symlinks are copies; dangling links are impossible |
+| 97 | extrac14 | Symlinks are copies (passes with `MSYS=winsymlinks:nativestrict` on both) |
+| 103 | extrac20 | Symlinks are copies (passes with nativestrict on both) |
+| 108 | extrac25 | Dangling symlink cannot be created |
+| 117 | incr01 | Dangling symlink cannot be created |
+| 148 | link04 | Symlinks are copies (passes with nativestrict on both) |
+| 155 | time01 | Windows file times cannot go earlier than 1601 |
+
+The 36 skipped tests need features this host does not have: lzip, lzop, xattrs, ACLs,
+SELinux, capabilities, big files, or root.
+
+## Test Fixes Applied
+None. All tests behave the same as the x64 build, unmodified.
+
+## Benchmark Results
+- **Result file**: `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`.
+- **Executed on**: the native ARM64 host. Other workloads were running at the same time,
+  so treat the numbers as indicative.
+
+| Operation (196 MiB tree) | ARM64 tar (native) | x64 tar (emulated) |
+|---|---|---|
+| `tar -cf` | 0.43-0.45 s | 0.43-0.51 s |
+| `tar -xf` | 0.61-0.64 s | 0.68-0.70 s |
+| `tar -czf` | 9.70-9.95 s | 6.21-6.49 s |
+| `tar -xzf` | 1.13-1.28 s | 0.90-1.06 s |
+
+Plain tar is at parity or slightly faster on ARM64. The whole gzip gap comes from the
+external ARM64 `gzip` binary: gzip alone took 9.94 s on ARM64 and 6.17 s on x64. tar
+itself does not cause it.
+
+## NEON Optimizations
+Phase 7 was skipped because `WOS_SKIP_OPTIMIZE` was set. tar also has no SIMD code or
+compute hot path; compression runs in external programs.
+
+## ARM64 vs x64 Performance Comparison
+No x64 benchmark reference file was supplied, so a differential comparison does not apply.
+The informal side-by-side timing is shown under Benchmark Results.
+
+## Architecture Verification
+All built binaries were verified with `dumpbin /HEADERS` from MSVC 14.51
+(HostARM64\ARM64):
+
+| Binary | Machine | Size (bytes) |
+|---|---|---|
+| build-arm64/src/tar.exe | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 608009 |
+| build-arm64/rmt/rmt.exe | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 82860 |
+| build-arm64/tests/genfile.exe | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 133069 |
+| build-arm64/tests/checkseekhole.exe | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 21743 |
+| build-arm64/tests/ckmtime.exe | AA64 machine (ARM64) | 23277 |
+
+The runtime dependencies in the sysroot are also AA64: `msys-2.0.dll`, `msys-iconv-2.dll`,
+`msys-intl-8.dll` and `sh.exe`.
+
+## Arm AppReady Status
+- **Target profile**: ARM64-native (`aarch64-pc-cygwin` / MSYS2 runtime).
+- **AppReady stages reached**: Assess done, Build done, Deploy not applicable (packaged by
+  the MSYS2 recipe), Optimize skipped (WOS_SKIP_OPTIMIZE).
+- **Dependencies**:
+
+| Dependency | Status | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| msys2-runtime (`msys-2.0.dll`) | native ARM64 | aarch64 runtime build, AA64 |
+| libiconv | native ARM64 | sysroot `msys-iconv-2.dll`, AA64 |
+| libintl (gettext) | native ARM64 | sysroot `msys-intl-8.dll`, AA64 |
+| sh (bash) | native ARM64 | sysroot `sh.exe`, AA64 |
+
+- **Emulation**: none. All components run natively.
+- **App Assure blockers**: none.
+
+## Limitations & Known Issues
+None. All reachable limitations were resolved.
+
+The 10 failing tests are Windows/MSYS filesystem design facts (filename characters,
+symlink emulation, `noacl` permissions, pre-1601 timestamps). They are identical on x64,
+so they are not port defects.
+
+## Reverting / Coexistence
+The x64 build is unchanged. To build x64, use `main` with the normal MSYS2 recipe
+(`--build=x86_64-pc-msys`, no `--host`).
